		{
			"id": "111211560304497702",
			"parentId": "111211231375442677",
			"url": "https://social.bennypowers.dev/@bp/111211560254166007",
			"author": {
				"name": "Benny Powers 🇨🇦️🇮🇱️",
				"url": "https://social.bennypowers.dev/@bp",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T16:02:19.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Yeah I know, but like... what if we built a generation of tools that *didn't* fight against current and future standards? What if we implemented ideas like HTML progressive enhancement of web components in the way in which *browser authors have recommended*? Wouldn't that be really nice? Wouldn't that let us update our tools and projects much more smoothly in the future? Wouldn't that make it so much easier to transfer knowledge between projects and prevent name conflicts?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111211564572594584",
			"parentId": "111211291437410860",
			"url": "https://social.bennypowers.dev/@bp/111211564529739109",
			"author": {
				"name": "Benny Powers 🇨🇦️🇮🇱️",
				"url": "https://social.bennypowers.dev/@bp",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T16:03:24.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@brianleroux\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>brianleroux</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> that's an opinion. GNOME web for example doesn't even *let* you disable javascript globally, because they observed that nobody does.</p><p>A few months of waiting is worth not building a generation of tools which improperly implement spec'd behaviour</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111211571847240082",
			"parentId": "111211564572594584",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@brianleroux/111211571652696406",
			"author": {
				"name": "Brian LeRoux 💚",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@brianleroux",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/314/763/370/860/389/original/b7637f3827245164.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T16:05:13.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://social.bennypowers.dev/@bp\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>bp</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> gnome may not let you disable js but it will still fail and then those users will have a terrible experience. It's about professional baselines not blindly implementing specs before they are ubiquitous. Standards based dev is about including everyone not just ppl who got lucky with a page load.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111211573093737387",
			"parentId": "111211560304497702",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/111211573093737387",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T16:05:35.146Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://social.bennypowers.dev/@bp\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>bp</span></a></span> browser authors aren’t #1 on this list, which is typically what I go by <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/html-design-principles/#priority-of-constituencies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">w3.org/TR/html-design-principl</span><span class=\"invisible\">es/#priority-of-constituencies</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111211587141355903",
			"parentId": "111211571847240082",
			"url": "https://social.bennypowers.dev/@bp/111211587110217199",
			"author": {
				"name": "Benny Powers 🇨🇦️🇮🇱️",
				"url": "https://social.bennypowers.dev/@bp",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T16:09:09.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@brianleroux\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>brianleroux</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>```html<br>&lt;c-e&gt;<br>&lt;template shadowrootmode=\"open\"&gt;<br>  &lt;style&gt;<br>    :host:not(:defined) ::slotted(<a href=\"https://social.bennypowers.dev/tags/fallback\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>fallback</span></a>) { /* 🎉️ */ } <br>  &lt;/style&gt;<br>&lt;/template&gt;<br>&lt;div id=\"fallback\" slot=\"fallback\"&gt;<br>&lt;noscript&gt;fallback content&lt;/noscript&gt;<br>&lt;/div&gt;<br>&lt;/c-e&gt;<br>```</p><p>season to taste</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
