			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T16:33:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Actually just published something this morning and gave a nod to this toot cause I called what I did \"web components\" but it's really just a custom element with full markup over the wire which then gets enhanced/added to by the custom element's JS (if its available). Didn't have a word for it so just said \"it's a web component”</p><p><a href=\"https://blog.jim-nielsen.com/2023/web-components-icon-galleries/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">blog.jim-nielsen.com/2023/web-</span><span class=\"invisible\">components-icon-galleries/</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
