			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T20:43:44.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@westbrook\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>westbrook</span></a></span> I'd give a +1 to having a classification between the two. At this point I think \"web components\" has (imo) been pretty heavily marketed/discussed as being the *combination* of CEs, shadow dom, templates, and {insert other WIP APIs} whereas I usually call what Zach is describing as \"wrapping markup with custom elements to declaratively define interactive UI\"</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111212821980296879",
			"parentId": "111212666862891028",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@westbrook/111212821953827922",
			"author": {
				"name": "westbrook",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@westbrook",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/292/789/947/647/037/original/03d44aaa7398e979.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T21:23:11.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@hawkticehurst\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>hawkticehurst</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> where so you specifically place the delta between the two?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111213351721713787",
			"parentId": "111212821980296879",
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@hawkticehurst/111213351706491458",
			"author": {
				"name": "Hawk Ticehurst",
				"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@hawkticehurst",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/382/229/410/239/377/original/4b2b3ec1efe031b4.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T23:37:54.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@westbrook\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>westbrook</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> In this case I'd say the delta is CEs versus all other WC APIs</p><p>If we formally call what Zach is describing \"web components\" I worry it risks muddying what that term means. Most docs/resources describe WCs as being the combo of CEs, shadow dom, and templates (+ others) but what Zach is talking about is just using the CE API</p><p>In my mind it's about being precise with wording and also thinking about all the docs/resources that already exist if that makes sense?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111213367102488039",
			"parentId": "111213351721713787",
			"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@hawkticehurst/111213367078593801",
			"author": {
				"name": "Hawk Ticehurst",
				"url": "https://fosstodon.org/@hawkticehurst",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/382/229/410/239/377/original/4b2b3ec1efe031b4.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-10-10T23:41:49.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@westbrook\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>westbrook</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Also to be clear, I don't think it would be wrong/bad to casually or informally describe this as \"web components\" but for the purposes of education/docs I think being precise that this a method of building interactive UI using only custom elements and nothing else from the \"web component\" bucket of APIs is probably a smart move</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111337500465675795",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.nz/@mez/111337500283402537",
			"author": {
				"name": "Philip (is looking for work)",
				"url": "https://mastodon.nz/@mez",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/322/213/008/546/280/original/716603c4d65ea709.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-01T21:50:31.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Wait, I thought this was just \"web components\"? Is this not the default usage and anything Shadowy or requiring dependencies it the exception? Who is doing the reverse?</p><p>/cc <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jimniels\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jimniels</span></a></span> since I found this toot via his icon site blog post</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111337784755081310",
			"parentId": "111337500465675795",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/111337784755081310",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-01T23:02:52.264Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.nz/@mez\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>mez</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jimniels\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>jimniels</span></a></span> as someone that remembers going through this revelation and then seeing it replay a few times now, I think my personal anecdata suggests otherwise</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111338151437664388",
			"parentId": "111337784755081310",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@jimniels/111338151408183666",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jim Nielsen",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@jimniels",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/524/723/264/449/500/original/c38868fb7e6df44b.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-02T00:36:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.nz/@mez\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mez</span></a></span> yeah I always thought of “web components” as the entire suite of technologies (custom elements, shadow dom, es modules, &lt;slot&gt;, etc.)</p><p>For me personally, I would love to have a term I could use to differentiate between web components that are used in a progressively enhanced way, eg</p><p>&lt;app-drawer&gt;<br>  &lt;nav&gt;<br>    &lt;a&gt;…&lt;/a&gt;<br>    &lt;a&gt;…&lt;/a&gt;<br>  &lt;/nav&gt;<br>&lt;app-drawer&gt;</p><p>Instead of something like:</p><p>&lt;app-drawer&gt;&lt;/app-drawer&gt;</p><p>With a bunch of JS</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111338245768850312",
			"parentId": "111338151437664388",
			"url": "https://mastodon.nz/@mez/111338245484143079",
			"author": {
				"name": "Philip (is looking for work)",
				"url": "https://mastodon.nz/@mez",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/322/213/008/546/280/original/716603c4d65ea709.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-02T01:00:02.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jimniels\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jimniels</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Gotcha. I think I was just slow on the uptake so I didn’t get much further than custom elements. I also am not in a spot where I’m building things for public consumption or re-use across different client projects.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111372617965009325",
			"parentId": "111212114198813779",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@McNeely/111372617948717681",
			"author": {
				"name": "McNeely",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@McNeely",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/552/212/183/557/481/original/75a9716caf3885be.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-08T02:41:24.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jimniels\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jimniels</span></a></span> late to the conversation since I just read Jim's post but it seems like the important parts of the convention are 1) it's just light DOM 2) it's  progressively enhanced HTML. With those two thoughts in mind I think either a name like \"Enhanced Components\" or \"Progressive Tags\" might work for classifying the technique.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
